# Planning Context

Invoke this rule only when planning a milestone. Implementation turns must not
load it.

## Read exactly once

1. `docs/context/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` - mission, scope, non-goals.
2. `docs/context/ARCHITECTURE.md` - layers, flows, runtime placement.
3. `docs/context/SAFETY_INVARIANTS.md` - non-negotiable live-safety properties.
4. `docs/context/DOMAIN_CONTRACTS.md` - typed messages and state machines.
5. `docs/context/DATA_SPEC.md` - data, quality, calculation, replay.
6. `docs/context/BROKER_SPEC.md` - adapter, order, reconciliation behavior.
7. `docs/context/TESTING_AND_RELEASE.md` - evidence and promotion gates.
8. `docs/context/OPERATIONS_RUNBOOK.md` - readiness and remediation.
9. `docs/context/POC_ROADMAP.md` - safe vertical build order.
10. `docs/context/CURRENT_STATE.md` - evidence-backed status.
11. Only the relevant `docs/context/STRATEGY_SPECS/` file.

Then inspect the actual repository with `rg`. Do not trust
`CURRENT_STATE.md` over observed files.

## Produce

Write `docs/plans/ACTIVE_PLAN.md` as a compact digest: goal, scope, non-goals,
context digest, vertical slices with exact files and acceptance tests,
unresolved decisions, residual risks. Populate `docs/plans/TASK_LEDGER.md` with
exactly one `READY` item.

Set `PLAN_STATUS: APPROVED`, increment `CONTEXT_DIGEST_VERSION`, and set
`CONTEXT_REFRESH_REQUIRED: no` only after the user approves.

## Rules

Build one vertical slice, not disconnected placeholders. Respect the roadmap
order; do not pull a later phase forward. Record unresolved decisions
explicitly rather than choosing a default and hiding it in code.
